  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I need to find:\n1. The background color, the 0-shape, and a colored pixel\n2. Direction from nearest 0-cell to colored pixel\n3. The spacing for stamping copies, determined by finding the minimum step where the translated shape doesn't create overlapping offset-differences with the original\n\nThe key insight is computing all pairwise differences of shape offsets, then finding the smallest multiple of the direction vector that falls outside this difference set.\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    from collections import Counter\n    flat = [c for row in grid for c in row]\n    bg = Counter(flat).most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    zero_cells = []\n    colored_pixel = None\n    colored_color = None\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0:\n                zero_cells.append((r, c))\n            elif grid[r][c] != bg:\n                colored_pixel = (r, c)\n                colored_color = grid[r][c]\n    \n    if not zero_cells or colored_pixel is None:\n        return grid\n    \n    cr = round(sum(r for r, c in zero_cells) / len(zero_cells))\n    cc = round(sum(c for r, c in zero_cells) / len(zero_cells))\n    shape_offsets = [(r - cr, c - cc) for r, c in zero_cells]\n    \n    pr, pc = colored_pixel\n    nearest = min(zero_cells, key=lambda z: (z[0]-pr)**2 + (z[1]-pc)**2)\n    dr = pr - nearest[0]\n    dc = pc - nearest[1]\n    \n    diffs = set()\n    for q in shape_offsets:\n        for o in shape_offsets:\n            diffs.add((q[0]-o[0], q[1]-o[1]))\n    \n    n_step = 1\n    while (n_step * dr, n_step * dc) in diffs:\n        n_step += 1\n    \n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    zero_set = set(zero_cells)\n    \n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        stamp_r = cr + k * n_step * dr\n        stamp_c = cc + k * n_step * dc\n        any_in_bounds = False\n        for off_r, off_c in shape_offsets:\n            sr = stamp_r + off_r\n            sc = stamp_c + off_c\n            if 0 <= sr < rows and 0 <= sc < cols:\n                any_in_bounds = True\n                if (sr, sc) not in zero_set:\n                    result[sr][sc] = colored_color\n        if not any_in_bounds:\n            break\n        k += 1\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    from collections import Counter\n    flat = [c for row in grid for c in row]\n    bg = Counter(flat).most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    zero_cells = []\n    colored_pixel = None\n    colored_color = None\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0:\n                zero_cells.append((r, c))\n            elif grid[r][c] != bg:\n                colored_pixel = (r, c)\n                colored_color = grid[r][c]\n    \n    if not zero_cells or colored_pixel is None:\n        return grid\n    \n    cr = round(sum(r for r, c in zero_cells) / len(zero_cells))\n    cc = round(sum(c for r, c in zero_cells) / len(zero_cells))\n    shape_offsets = [(r - cr, c - cc) for r, c in zero_cells]\n    \n    pr, pc = colored_pixel\n    nearest = min(zero_cells, key=lambda z: (z[0]-pr)**2 + (z[1]-pc)**2)\n    dr = pr - nearest[0]\n    dc = pc - nearest[1]\n    \n    diffs = set()\n    for q in shape_offsets:\n        for o in shape_offsets:\n            diffs.add((q[0]-o[0], q[1]-o[1]))\n    \n    n_step = 1\n    while (n_step * dr, n_step * dc) in diffs:\n        n_step += 1\n    \n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    zero_set = set(zero_cells)\n    \n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        stamp_r = cr + k * n_step * dr\n        stamp_c = cc + k * n_step * dc\n        any_in_bounds = False\n        for off_r, off_c in shape_offsets:\n            sr = stamp_r + off_r\n            sc = stamp_c + off_c\n            if 0 <= sr < rows and 0 <= sc < cols:\n                any_in_bounds = True\n                if (sr, sc) not in zero_set:\n                    result[sr][sc] = colored_color\n        if not any_in_bounds:\n            break\n        k += 1\n    \n    return result",
